ChatDataset: accept the NeMo Platform's SFT chat rows (separate ``thinking`` messages, tool results
without ``tool_call_id``).

The platform's SFT chat schema (``SFTChatMessage``, ``extra="forbid"``) keeps an assistant turn's reasoning
in a message of its own, ``{"role": "assistant", "thinking": "..."}``, and its ``tool`` messages carry only
``role`` and ``content``. ``ChatDataset._normalize_messages`` expects the OpenAI shape, so rows from the
platform failed two ways:

- A ``thinking`` message was not recognised. It rendered as an empty assistant turn
  (``<think>\n\n</think>``) and its reasoning never reached the model.
- A ``tool`` message without ``tool_call_id`` raised "tool message `tool_call_id` must be a non-empty
  string", because ``__getitem__`` normalizes every row.

Now a ``thinking`` message is folded into ``reasoning_content`` on the assistant message after it (or kept as
its own assistant message when none follows), and a ``tool`` message without an id takes the id of the next
unanswered tool call of the assistant message before it, in call order. Rows that already use
``reasoning_content`` and ``tool_call_id`` are unchanged.

Applies after automodel-chat-dataset-tool-call-arguments.patch (same function). Drop this patch once the
pinned Automodel commit includes the change.

